on the current bars."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window covers 120 closed D1 bars from 1779667200000 to 1790035199999; window low 1368.42 (bar 13), window high 2850 (bar 120).", "Bars 1-13 sell off from 2139.34 (bar 1 high) to 1368.42 (bar 13 low), -36.0%; bar 13 (O1581.32 H1599.27 L1368.42 C1568.55) closes with a 200.13-point lower tail, and bar 14 (O1568.55 H1690.78 L1563.52 C1687.83) is a large bull bar closing near its high.", "Bars 14-86 build a 73-bar base between 1512.91 (bar 33 low) and 1974.46 (bar 64 high) with dense bar overlap and rising lows in the second half (1694.74 bar 40, 1821.49 bar 71, 1868.42 bar 78, 1875.03 bar 83).", "Bar 87 (O1916.51 H2293.8 L1905.63 C2252.16) is a bull spike bar with a 335.65 body, about +17.5% from its open, closing 41.64 below its high; bar 88 closes 2326.32; bar 89 spikes to 2771 and closes 2515.30 with a 255.70 upper tail.", "Bars 90-116 form a 27-bar range between 2357.18 (bar 101 low) and 2680 (bar 110 high); most bars trade 2386-2557 with repeated upside probes closing back inside: bar 110 H2680/C2514.72, bar 113 H2609.02/C2514.07, bar 118 H2700/C2632.98.", "Bars 117-120 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 and 2775.61, each above the prior close, starting from bar 117's 2446.22 open.", "Bar 120 (O2642.9 H2850 L2641.7 C2775.61) has a 208.3 range, a 132.71 bull body, closes at 64% of its range with a 74.39 upper tail; the close 2775.61 is 75.61 above the post-spike range high 2700 and 4.61 above the window's prior high 2771.", "Ordered read: bear selloff, long base, bull spike out of that base, 27-bar consolidation holding above the spike low, then a four-bar push to new window highs."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening bear selloff from the window high 2139.34 (bar 1) to 1368.42 (bar 13 low): 13 bars of mostly lower closes with ranges expanding to 230.85 on bar 13, whose 200.13 lower tail shows sellers giving up the low; immediately reversed by the large bull bar 14.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1779667200000, "upper_boundary": "2139.34"}, {"description": "Long base/consolidation after the selloff, 1512.91 (bar 33 low) to 1974.46 (bar 64 high). Bars 14-38 chop roughly 1550-1845; bars 39-86 drift up with higher lows and repeated tests of 1900-1975; heavy overlap throughout, typical range behavior.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Three-bar bull spike out of the base. Bar 87 (O1916.51 H2293.8 L1905.63 C2252.16) is a 335.65-body bull trend bar closing 41.64 below its high; bar 88 closes 2326.32; bar 89 spikes to 2771 and closes 2515.30, leaving a 255.70 upper tail.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "27-bar two-sided range following the spike, 2357.18 (bar 101 low) to 2680 (bar 110 high). Dense overlap; the bulk of bars trade 2386-2557 and each upside probe closes back inside (bar 110 H2680/C2514.72, bar 113 H2609.02/C2514.07, bar 118 H2700/C2632.98).", "end_time_ms": 1789603199999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Current four-bar up leg and upside breakout attempt above the 27-bar range: closes 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 and 2775.61 from bar 117's 2446.22 open. Bar 120 (O2642.9 H2850 L2641.7 C2775.61) closes above the range high 2700 and 4.61 above the window's prior high 2771, but 74.39 below its own high, so acceptance is not yet shown.", "end_time_ms": 1790035199999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Bull continuation: a close above 2850, or a second consecutive close above 2771 with the bar closing in its upper third, would confirm acceptance above the range and support trend continuation.", "Failed breakout: a close back below 2700, and especially below 2680 (bar 110 high), re-entering the 2357.18-2680 range, would mark bar 120's push as a failed breakout, particularly if the bar closes near its low.", "Range continuation: continued overlap with highs capped near 2771-2850 and no new closing high would keep the phase as range and shift the regime read toward trading-range.", "Trend damage: a close below 2436.87 (bar 117 low) negates the four-bar leg; a close below 2357.18 (bar 101 low) ends the post-spike higher-low sequence and turns the read to transition-unclear or trading-range.", "Deep failure: acceptance below 2111 (bar 88 low) would invalidate the spike structure and return the pre-spike base to relevance."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "stale"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790107199999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Bar 112 has a 126.85 upper tail and closes 2723.15, below its 2754.03 midpoint, a weak close for a 191.94-range spike bar and a possible buy-climax/exhaustion signature.", "Bars 113-120 overlap heavily, none closes above 2775.61, and the latest high 2804.59 is a lower high versus 2850, so the immediate eight-bar structure is genuinely two-sided rather than trending.", "This window shows two prior vertical spikes that were fully retraced: bar 53 high 2680 preceded a 321.38 drop to 2358.62, and bar 73 high 2609.02 (a marginal new high over 2607.62) preceded a 250.40 sell-off, so spike-and-fail is a repetitive behavior here.", "The whole window contains two long range sections (42 bars in 2411.04-2537.57 and roughly 20 bars in 2440-2610), so the trend component is interleaved with substantial rotation rather than a clean one-way market."], "evidence_for": ["Net window change is strongly upward (open 2391.63 to close 2749.43) and the window high 2850 was set only 9 bars before the end, so the dominant direction over the supplied window is up.", "Higher swing lows since 2358.62 (2384.29, 2435.71, 2569.80, 2658.06, 2716.01) with matching higher highs (2585.50, 2643.52, 2700, 2850) satisfy the standard bull trend progression on this window.", "The up-leg contains genuine spike bars closing near their highs (bar 95 close 2578.60 vs high 2585.50; bar 96 close 2636.28 vs high 2643.52; bar 112 broke above the 2700 equal highs), not just overlapping drift.", "The current pullback held: bar 117 low 2716.01 is above the 2700.00 breakout zone and none of bars 113-120 closed below bar 112's 2658.06 low, so the last pause has not yet damaged the trend structure.", "The earlier mid-trend pause (bars 97-106, 2568.16-2646.36) resolved upward with bars 107-112, showing this window's pattern of pause-then-continuation within the bull leg."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars from 1788379200000 to 1790107199999: open 2391.63 -> close 2749.43 (+357.80, about +15.0%), highest high 2850 (bar 112, 1789977600000), lowest low 2358.62 (bar 78, 1789488000000).", "Bars 1-10 rallied from 2377.88 to 2537.57 (bar 10 high), with bar 5 (open 2407.48, high 2509.15, close 2506.79) as a wide bull spike closing near its high.", "Bars 11-52 (1788523200000-1789127999999) were a 42-bar trading range between 2411.04 (bar 47 low) and 2537.57 (bar 10 high), with repeated 2527-2537 highs failing (bar 11 low 2436.73, bar 21 high 2527.29, bar 26 high 2528.80).", "Bar 53 (open 2457.12, high 2680, low 2444.19, close 2555.52) spiked out of that range, closing 111.33 above its low but leaving a 124.48 upper tail.", "Bars 54-78 formed a near-double top: bar 54 high 2607.62 and bar 73 high 2609.02, with bar 73 (open 2540.11, close 2514.07) closing near its low, followed by a bear leg to 2358.62 (bar 78), 250.40 below 2609.02.", "Since bar 78 the sequence is higher highs and higher lows: lows 2384.29 (bar 83), 2435.71 (bar 89), 2569.80 (bar 104), 2658.06 (bar 112), 2716.01 (bar 117); highs 2585.50 (bar 95), 2643.52 (bar 96), 2700 (bars 100 and 110, equal highs), 2850 (bar 112), 2804.59 (bar 115).", "Bull spike bars close near their highs in the up-leg: bar 95 (2507.15->2578.60, low 2495.82), bar 96 (2579.97->2636.28, low 2578.44), and bar 112 (open 2658.81, low 2658.06, high 2850, close 2723.15).", "Bar 112 is a 191.94-range bar with a 126.85 upper tail and a close 30.88 below its 2754.03 midpoint, i.e. a wide spike bar with a weak close.", "Bars 113-120 (1789992000000-1790107199999) all trade inside bar 112's range: highs 2795, 2770.03, 2804.59, 2776.18, 2741.20, 2752.61, 2761.62, 2761.63; lows 2718.09, 2734.22, 2759.63, 2727.22, 2716.01, 2722.76, 2722.62, 2729.14; closes 2754.31, 2760.51, 2775.61, 2738.87, 2724.95, 2740.20, 2742.31, 2749.43.", "The eight-bar pullback low 2716.01 (bar 117) holds above the 2700.00 equal-high breakout zone, so the last pause has not retraced into the prior consolidation (2568.16-2646.36 in bars 97-106) and no bar has closed below 2658.06 (bar 112 low).", "No bar since 2850 has exceeded the prior high; the latest high 2804.59 (bar 115) is a lower high and the final bar 120 (open 2742.31, high 2761.63, low 2729.14, close 2749.43) sits mid-range, not at a boundary, so no active boundary test is in progress."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "42-bar trading range between 2411.04 (bar 47 low) and 2537.57 (bar 10 high); repeated pushes to 2527-2537 were rejected and overlap was heavy.", "end_time_ms": 1789127999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2411.04", "start_time_ms": 1788523200000, "upper_boundary": "2537.57"}, {"description": "Bull spike bar 53 broke the ~2530 range top and closed at 2555.52 wi